<title>RUSSIA: LUKoil details '96 financial, output data.</title>
<headline>LUKoil details '96 financial, output data.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>LUKoil, Russia's largest oil company, posted net profits of 3.84 trillion roubles in 1996 on a cash basis and to Russian accounting standards, up 60 percent from 2.40 trillion in 1995, the company said Thursday.</p>
<p>The figures appeared in the company's annual report issued at the annual shareholders' meeting, and represented slight revisions from financial results given previously by LUKoil.</p>
<p>They are also the final results for 1995 and 1996, LUKoil spokeman Pyotr Neyev said.</p>
<p>The company gave the following financial and production data for 1996 and 1995  --</p>
<p>LUKOIL FINANCIAL RESULTS AND PRODUCTION DATA, 1995 AND 1996</p>
<p>						 1996		1995</p>
<p> Net profit (trln roubles)	    3.842	     2.404</p>
<p> Net profit (million dollars)		 750		 528</p>
<p> Net sales (trln roubles)	    44.015	    23.421</p>
<p> Net sales (million dollars)		8,595	     5,144</p>
<p> Year-end assets (trln roubles)    69.347	    44.082</p>
<p> Year-end assets (million dollars)     12,472	     9,500</p>
<p>Oil production (million tonnnes)</p>
<p>  (inc. joint ventures)		  58.5		57.3</p>
<p> Oil refining (million tonnes)	     19.3		19.0</p>
<p>Oil exports (million tonnes)</p>
<p>  (inc. joint ventures)		  16.5		18.4</p>
<p> Product exports (million tonnes)	   4.5		 2.3</p>
<p> Number of employees		   94,200	   106,900</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
